{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Come to Pharaoh</b> — when He would tell him to come to his house, He would say to him \"come,\" and when He would tell him to go to him at the river, He would say to him \"go.\"" "<b>בא</b> rises in gematria to 3, hinting to him: 3 plagues He will yet bring upon him." "<b>שתי</b> — three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: שיתי כליל צלך (Isaiah 32:8), שתי לבך למסלה (Proverbs 23:19). Teaching that even though he did not warn him explicitly about the plague of darkness, he hinted to him — and this is שיתי כליל צלך — and to Israel He said שתי לבך למסלה, that they prepare themselves and search in the Egyptians' houses during the days of darkness to see their vessels, that they ask them for their vessels when they go. למען שתי — written defective, qere with yud: שתי, hinting at 2 plagues besides the plague of the firstborn, which He had already hinted to him in בוהנה לא שמעת עד כה (Exodus 11:9)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads המימה, literally 'the water' or 'the river'; I read it as 'at the river/water,' referring to Pharaoh's morning visits to the Nile (Exodus 7:15, 8:16).", 2 "I read שיתי for שיתו in the Isaiah citation (שיתו כליל צלך, Isaiah 32:8), following the masoretic juxtaposition the author draws. The phrase בוהנה לא שמעת עד כה appears to quote Exodus 11:9 (ולמען תספר ... את אשר התללתי במצרים) conflated with 10:1 (בעבור תספר ... את אשר התללתי); the two-letter form may abbreviate התללתי. The phrase may be corrupt; translated hyper-literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:32.975604959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}